eight / 2.0)))"]},"fault":{"label":"Illustration: a hand-made fault, not a real model run.","intro":"A block with a small peg on top. One line was edited by hand: the peg turns the wrong way.","verdicts":{"correct":{"label":"Correct","meaning":"Matches the target at this point."},"cause":{"label":"First error","meaning":"Its input matched the target but its output does not, so the blame lands here."},"inherited":{"label":"Inherited","meaning":"Already wrong on arrival; the difference was carried in from an earlier step, not caused here."}},"ops":[{"short":"Sketch plane","verdict":"correct","state":"Nothing built yet, only a reference plane. Same as the target."},{"short":"Base block","verdict":"correct","state":"The base block exists and matches the target's base."},{"short":"Sketch plane","verdict":"correct","state":"Base unchanged; a new plane is ready for the peg."},{"short":"Peg block","verdict":"correct","state":"Base plus a peg of the right size, still matching the target."},{"short":"Rotate peg","verdict":"cause","state":"The peg is turned the wrong way because the angle's sign is flipped. Everything matched before this step, so this is where the part first goes wrong."},{"short":"Move peg","verdict":"inherited","state":"The move itself is right, but the peg still carries the wrong turn from the step before."},{"short":"Join parts","verdict":"inherited","state":"The finished part looks close to the target, but the peg is still turned the wrong way."}]},"parts":[{"name":"Write code","status":"built","status_text":"Built","sentence":"A frozen language model writes a CadQuery program from the text request; its weights are never changed."},{"name":"Run in sandbox","status":"built","status_text":"Built","sentence":"The program runs in an isolated sandbox and returns a solid or an error."},{"name":"Intermediate representation","status":"partial","status_text":"Partial, experiment pending","sentence":"The program is turned into a feature tree plus the solid after every operation; whether this helps repair is still being tested."},{"name":"Outcome check","status":"built","status_text":"Built","sentence":"Compares the final shape with the target and names the kind of mismatch, such as a misplaced or missing feature."},{"name":"Process verifier","status":"built","status_text":"Built, tested on hand-made faults only","sentence":"Walks the operations in order and blames the first one whose output stops matching the target."},{"name":"Repair packet","status":"partial","status_text":"Partial","sentence":"Turns the evidence into plain parts for the model: what is wrong, where in the code, a suggested fix, and what to keep."},{"name":"Repeat, keep the best","status":"built","status_text":"Built, ground-truth-guided","sentence":"The model rewrites its code from the packet, up to 3 turns; the best attempt is kept and the loop stops early once the part is right."},{"name":"Learn cards","status":"partial","status_text":"Partial, offline only","sentence":"Offline, failed and repaired training samples are checked against their ground truth and distilled into short reusable repair cards."},{"name":"Reuse cards","status":"partial","status_text":"Partial, not wired into the live loop","sentence":"Later runs would look up cards that match the current fault and add their advice to the repair prompt; this is not connected to the live loop yet."}],"text":{"titles":["The model writes code, and we check the part after every step.","Watch the part get built, one step at a time.","Comparing step by step finds the first mistake.","One repair that worked.","What is still missing."],"loop":["Write code","Run it","Compare to the target","Tell the model what is wrong","Try again a few times, keeping the best"],"frozen":"The language model stays frozen: we never retrain it. Only the feedback changes.","gt":"Right now the repair is guided by the ground-truth shape.","snap":"The representation keeps this snapshot at every step.","aligned":"Shapes aligned for display, simplified for the page.","change":"What changed: the first attempt put both circles in one sketch and pushed them up together, so the overlap never merged into one clean solid. The repair made each circle its own cylinder, then joined the two.","caption":"One sample, chosen because it worked. Repair was scored against the ground-truth shape. This run scored five attempts, more than the current loop allows.","cards":"Repair cards are short notes on how a past mistake was fixed.","views":[["Target","The target: two overlapping upright cylinders merged into one solid."],["First attempt","The first attempt: two overlapping cylinders that were never merged into one solid."],["After repair","After repair: two cylinders joined into one solid, close to the target."]],"missing":[["partial","Partial","Reusing repair cards","Works offline, not in the live loop."],["proposed","Proposed","Repair without the ground-truth shape","One small pilot."],["proposed","Proposed","Process verifier on real model mistakes","Tested on hand-made faults only."]]}}